 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "During my inspection, I noted that the front bumper is misaligned on the passenger side. The exterior of the vehicle was wet, which can obscure minor imperfections. There are minor miscellaneous scratches around the vehicle. I observed two 2-inch scratches on the rear bumper. Additionally, I noticed a dent on the left quarter panel and observed filler in the right rear quarter panel with an unpainted area. According to the paint gauge, the right rear door has been repainted. The hood and rear bumper displayed stone chips, and the front bumper has a gouge. All wheels exhibited curb rash."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "I noticed moderate wear on the seats. The interior requires detailing or cleaning. Wear consistent with age and mileage was visible on the steering wheel, center console, inner door panels, and interior trim."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "I saw that the battery terminals are corroded, and I recommend a battery service to clean the terminals. The brake rotors are displaying signs of surface rust. The exhaust exhibits some surface rust, but currently, there are no leaks, and it sounds good. Additionally, the key fob is broken."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "A scan of the ECU found no current, pending, or historic fault codes. The vehicle started and idled normally. During warm-up, there was no excessive smoke or steam emission. I test drove the vehicle and the ride, acceleration, and handling felt normal. The engine was smooth and responsive. The transmission worked as designed without issues and the brakes exhibited firmness, with no noticeable pulsation. The TPMS (Tire Pressure Monitoring System) light is illuminated. Need further diagnosis."
  }
 ],
